On Dec 1, 9:35 pm, Sledgen <rs_sle...@hotmail.com> wrote:
> Given you have another WoW waiting for you at the castle you can
> definately afford whatever you need armourwise. A magic marker is
> definately a good idea. For armour, speed boots and a cloak of
> displacement are worthwhile.

Jumping boots are greatly preferrable to speed boots if you have
intrinsic "fast" (as a post-Quest valk he should); the difference from
"fast" to "very fast" just doesn't come close to jumping.

Displacement is only magic cancellation of 2, so a very bad idea for
someone going for their first ascension, IMO.

> Gauntlets of power are good for people of
> low experience but gauntlets of dexterity will do just as good.

Even leather is just as good (the dex doesn't matter much at all once
you max luck), and both leather and dex are much better if he wants to
cast (valks need to optimize carefully for that).  He's post-quest so
strength is already maxed or near it in all likelihood, so I really
doubt GoPower are worth a wish (and they might be actively bad if he
wants to cast spells or if they foolishly encourage him to throw mojo).


